  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 100 PM CDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nThursday-Monday:\nThe ridge and associated high pressure amplify into late week,\nsupporting further warming across the area. Highs through the\nweekend approach upper 70s to near 80 in most locations as\nsupported by 850mb temperatures around 13-16C. Additionally,\nless cloud cover is expected through the upcoming weekend as any\nshortwave energy becomes displaced well west of the region. This\nperiod of above normal temperatures (5 to 10 degrees) will be\naccompanied by dry weather through the weekend. Despite the warm\nand dry conditions, we are currently not expecting any elevated\nfire weather concerns through the weekend given the lack of a\nstrong wind component. Nonetheless, potential fire weather will\nneed to be monitored closely as we progress into mid-Fall with \ndrought conditions persisting. \n\nEnsemble guidance hint at a potential pattern change into next\nweek, though confidence remains low given the variability.\nFurther uncertainty exist in the temperatures into next week as\nNBM interquartile spreads increase to around 15 degrees.\nHowever, even the lower quartile would still support above\nnormal temperatures. Thus, confidence remains medium to high on\nabove normal temperatures through the end of October.",
